  "body": "With an outlook across tree-lined streets to Rangitoto and the sea, this substantial north-facing residence brings together impressive scale, refined design and low-maintenance luxury in a superb coastal setting. Bathed in natural light throughout the day, it offers beautifully considered spaces for family living, entertaining and hosting guests.  Spanning approximately 362sqm across three elevator-accessed levels, the home makes an immediate impression with a striking, light-filled atrium entrance and a cluster of dazzling glass sphere pendants. Oak timber flooring, crisp white interiors and expansive picture windows create a sophisticated coastal feel, with each level capturing its own unique outlook.\r\nGenerous living and dining spaces incorporate an efficient gas fireplace and built-in cabinetry, flowing seamlessly to balconies, decks and a covered patio protected by automatic roller blinds. At the heart of the home, the sleek designer kitchen is superbly equipped for entertaining, featuring a large island, multiple Miele wall ovens, stone benchtops and a full scullery with gas hob and butler sink.  All four bedrooms have beautifully appointed ensuite bathrooms, complemented by two separate guest powder rooms. A bedroom on the central level enjoys direct outdoor access, while upstairs a relaxed sitting area connects the main bedroom and another generous bedroom, both with walk-in wardrobes and panoramic views.\r\nDownstairs, a media lounge and guest bedroom provide excellent separation for family or visitors. A bespoke laundry, extensive storage and a spacious top-floor box room ensure the practicalities of family life are equally well catered for.  An internal-access double garage and ample forecourt parking complete the home, set on a fenced 416sqm (approx.) freehold site with established, sheltered gardens.\r\nZoned for Orakei School and Selwyn College, and conveniently located near Coates Avenue and Eastridge, this air-conditioned, double-glazed residence offers an impressive combination of space, quality and convenience, close to the city and some of Auckland's finest urban beaches.\r\n\r\nSee interactive features for this property on barfoot.co.nz. Click the \"View office website\" link at the bottom of this page.",
